    <string name="privacy_p1">TripMate is guest-first: trips, notes, expenses, journal and photos are stored locally on your device. No account is required.</string>
    <string name="privacy_p2">On-device AI (when your phone supports it) runs locally through Android AICore; prompts don’t leave the device.</string>
    <string name="privacy_p3">Cloud AI (Gemini via Firebase AI Logic) is used only after you allow it. TripMate sends the minimum needed: destination and place names, your question and schedule titles — never your account details or precise location. Photos and notes are sent only after explicit confirmation.</string>
    <string name="privacy_p4">AI answers can be wrong. Opening hours, prices, routes and accessibility are never presented as facts unless verified by a live source, and every AI answer shows where it came from.</string>
    <string name="privacy_p5">Location is requested only when you tap “I’m here”, used once in the foreground, and never tracked in the background or uploaded.</string>
    <string name="privacy_p6">You can export or permanently delete all your data from Settings at any time.</string>
